        "**RNA expression** shows which cells make a transcript, but the location of the protein must be measured directly. Corey and colleagues used an antibody against IR25a to determine where the protein sits. Cross-sections through distal aesthetasc hairs gave anatomical access to the outer dendrites, where transported odorants first approach olfactory neurons, so the antibody could be tested at the site of first contact with odor.",
